# Review Configuration
# Copy to your repo root as `review.md`, adapt, and commit it.
# Full schema: see the plugin's review-schema.md or run /reviewers:init to generate one.

## Settings
- output: .reviews/
- base: auto
- depth: module   # scope ladder per reviewer: function | file | module | domain

## Reviewer: Backend
- files: src/**, **/*.py
- guidelines: docs/python-style.md, docs/api-conventions.md
- focus: error handling, transaction safety, API contract stability

## Reviewer: DevOps
- files: Dockerfile*, .github/workflows/**, **/*.tf
- focus: reproducible builds, secret handling, rollback safety

## Reviewer: Technical Writing
- files: **/*.md, docs/**
- focus: accuracy against the code, terminology consistency, clarity

## Reviewer: Security
- always: true
- severity-floor: minor
- focus: injection, secrets, authn/authz, unsafe deserialization
